Building Vacuum-IM
==================

CMake is the supported build system. Run the commands below from the source
root. GitHub Actions is the supported CI service.

Requirements
------------
  * CMake 3.21 or newer, a C++17 compiler, and Ninja for the supplied presets.
  * Qt 6: Widgets, Network, Xml, Concurrent, LinguistTools, PrintSupport,
    Multimedia and Sql. Svg is optional.
  * Linux: Qt GuiPrivate development headers, X11 and XScreenSaver headers.
  * System zlib, minizip and libidn are used when found; otherwise bundled
    copies are built. QtLockedFile and QxtGlobalShortcut are always built from
    the bundled sources against the application's Qt version.
  * Hunspell is the preset spellchecker backend. A bundled copy is available
    if the system library is absent.
  * Optional: GStreamer 1.20+ with SDP and WebRTC development files for voice
    calls. Voice calls also
    need the webrtc, dtls, srtp, nice, opus and rtp runtime plugins.
  * Adium message styles are currently disabled: they require Qt WebKit,
    which is not available in Qt 6.

Linux
-----
Example build dependencies on Ubuntu 24.04:

  sudo apt install build-essential cmake ninja-build pkg-config \
    qt6-base-dev qt6-base-private-dev qt6-svg-dev qt6-multimedia-dev \
    qt6-tools-dev qt6-tools-dev-tools libgl-dev libx11-dev libxss-dev \
    zlib1g-dev libminizip-dev libidn-dev libhunspell-dev

Configure and build:

  cmake --preset release
  cmake --build --preset release --parallel

Install into a local staging directory:

  cmake --install build/release --prefix "$PWD/stage"
  ./stage/bin/vacuum

The installation contains bin/, lib/ and share/. Preserve this layout when
moving it. Linux builds use system Qt and other shared system libraries;
copying the installation tree does not bundle those dependencies.

A binary release needs a documented architecture, Linux/glibc baseline and
Qt build version. Qt's public API generally supports running binaries built
with an older Qt 6 on a newer Qt 6, not the reverse. The current X11 code uses
GuiPrivate APIs, so that general compatibility guarantee does not cover it:
use the matching distribution Qt build until that private dependency is
removed. Rebuilding from source uses the locally installed Qt version.

Windows
-------
Use a developer terminal for the compiler matching the installed Qt 6 kit
(for example, the x64 Visual Studio tools terminal for an MSVC x64 Qt kit).
Ensure Ninja is on PATH and point CMake at that Qt kit:

  cmake --preset release -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=C:/Qt/6.x.y/msvc2022_64 \
    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=C:/vacuum-stage
  cmake --build --preset release --parallel
  cmake --install build/release

The executable is installed as C:/vacuum-stage/vacuum/vacuum.exe. The same
configure/build/install commands can be used with a matching MinGW Qt kit.

Release packaging is being migrated to CMake/CPack and GitHub Actions. The
Windows release archive must include Qt plugins, compiler runtimes and all
other required dependencies so it runs immediately after extraction. The
Linux release archive will use system libraries. The source-build commands
above do not yet validate either release archive's deployment.

Development and configuration
-----------------------------
To run directly from the build directory:

  cmake --preset dev
  cmake --build --preset dev --parallel
  ./build/dev/vacuum

Presets are conveniences; other CMake generators remain supported:

  cmake -S . -B build/custom -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build/custom --config Release --parallel
  cmake --install build/custom --config Release --prefix /path/to/stage

Useful configure options (pass as -DNAME=value):

  INSTALL_SDK=ON                Install plugin development headers/helpers
                                (OFF in the supplied presets).
  INSTALL_DOCS=OFF              Skip installed documentation.
  INSTALL_LIB_DIR=lib64         Override the Unix library directory.
  PLUGIN_<name>=OFF             Disable a plugin, e.g. PLUGIN_voicecalls=OFF.
  SPELLCHECKER_BACKEND=HUNSPELL Select hunspell, enchant, aspell or macspell.
  LANGS="uk;de"                 Select translations (default: all languages).
  RUN_FROM_BUILD_DIR=ON         Use source resources and build-tree plugins.
  BUILD_TRANSLATION_TOOLS=ON    Build optional maintainer utilities.

For multi-configuration generators, always pass --config Release (or Debug)
when building and installing. Keep personal settings in CMakeUserPresets.json.

Translations and plugin maintenance
-----------------------------------
Normal builds compile enabled translations into .qm files and installation
copies them into the application tree. To compile only translations:

  cmake --build build/release --target translations

To update existing .ts files from the source (this modifies source files):

  cmake --build build/release --target updatets

Both targets honor LANGS and LANG_<language>. Per-component targets such as
updatets_vacuum and translations_vacuum are also available. Translation
synchronization scripts remain separate from the build.

Optional maintainer tools can be built with:

  cmake --preset release -DBUILD_TRANSLATION_TOOLS=ON
  cmake --build build/release --target autotranslate txprepare

The executables are in build/release/src/tools/ and are not installed with
the application. Run either without arguments for its usage.

To add a plugin, follow an existing plugin's CMakeLists.txt and source-list
.cmake file, then register its directory in src/plugins/plugin_list.cmake.
